# The tree is byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, so without this a Windows
# checkout gets CRLF everywhere - and this repo cannot survive that. The
# `.expected` and `.expected-errors` fixtures are compared against what a
# compiled program actually prints, which is LF; the corpus would fail on
# Windows for a reason that has nothing to do with the compiler. Forcing LF
# on checkout is what makes a Windows build the same build as a Linux one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries and archives are never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
